# Data fetching in apps/web

Pages own server state. Do not fetch in `useEffect`. Branch pending / empty / error in the page (Mantine `Skeleton` / `Alert`). Every non-docs API call waits **200–2000ms** and fails **~10%** of the time — keep round trips low. Do not invent URLs; use the Home Garden API skill.

## Ownership

```
SPA page (/gardens): queryOptions → page useQuery/useMutation → organism props
MPA page (/my-garden): static stub. No loader or query until the feature is implemented
```

- Put keys, `queryOptions`, and mutation fns in `app/queries/*`.
- Call `useQuery` / `useMutation` only in **SPA pages**.
- Pass results into organisms. Never `useQuery` in atoms, molecules, or templates.
- Use `api()` from `app/lib/api.ts` only. Name wrappers `<httpMethod><Resource>` (`getGardens`, `postGarden`). `queryOptions` factories stay `*Query`.

## QueryClient and round trips

Browser singleton via `getQueryClient()`. New client on the server. Never share a server client across requests.

Default `staleTime` is 60s. `retry: 2` in the app; **`retry: false` in tests**. Mutations `invalidateQueries` the resource parent key (`gardenKeys.all`, `plantKeys.byGarden(id)`).

Use one list call for a list. Start independent requests together (`useQueries`) when the id is already in the URL. Do not fetch per row, waterfall `queryFn`s, set `staleTime: 0`, or disable the API delay/error plugins.

## Agent do / don't

**Do**

- Use `useQuery(gardensQuery())` on `/gardens`
- Keep `/my-garden` a static stub until the feature is implemented
- Name every `api()` wrapper `<httpMethod><Resource>`

**Don't**

- `useEffect` + `fetch` / axios
- `useQuery` below the page layer, or on `/my-garden`
- Server-`loader` prefetch + `dehydrate` for gardens
- Fetch per row inside a list item

## Good / bad

```tsx
function GardensPanel() {
  const { data, isPending, isError, refetch } = useQuery(gardensQuery());
  if (isPending) return <GardenListSkeleton />;
  if (isError) {
    return (
      <Alert title="Could not load gardens" color="red">
        Something went wrong. Try again.
        <Button variant="primary" onClick={() => refetch()}>
          Retry
        </Button>
      </Alert>
    );
  }
  return <GardenList gardens={data} />;
}
```

```tsx
// Bad — useEffect fetch; per-row query
function GardenRow({ garden }: { garden: Garden }) {
  const plants = useQuery(plantsByGardenQuery(garden.gardenId));
  return <td>{plants.data?.length}</td>;
}
```
